%% FleetOS — Phase 5 feature-build dependency graph, per PROJECT_PLAN.md
%% "Suggested build order" + MASTER_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md Phase 5 table.
%% Updated after Cursor's independent review (round 2): Auth is built in
%% Phase 3, ahead of every module below — so uploadedBy/responsiblePerson/
%% authorId/notifications.userId become real FKs to users from their first
%% migration, not free text with a deferred cleanup. Notifications is no
%% longer "blocked," just built in its normal build-order position. Only
%% Settings' Users & Roles sub-page needs Auth — System Lists/General/
%% Company Profile/Form Requirements don't, so AUTH no longer gates all
%% of Settings the way it did in the previous version of this diagram.
%% Renumbered (round 3, after Cursor's review): PROJECT_PLAN.md's build
%% order moved Auth to step 0 and shifted every step below it down by one.
%% This diagram's node labels previously still showed the OLD numbers
%% (0=Ship Particulars ... 12=Dashboard) even though the comment above
%% already described Auth as built first — that mismatch is fixed below,
%% Auth is now labeled step 0 and every other label matches PROJECT_PLAN.md.
%% Added (this session): step 16, Email digest (PROJECT_PLAN.md §12b) —
%% appended after Export rather than inserted into the existing sequence,
%% to avoid triggering another renumbering pass across all three build-order
%% sources (see PLAN_REVIEW.md Round 3/4 for what happened last time).
flowchart LR
    V["Vessels\n(shipped)"]
    AUTH["0. Auth\n(= Phase 3, built FIRST\nusers/sessions exist before\nany Phase 5 table)"]
    SP["1. Ship Particulars"]
    ENG["2. Expiry/Reminder Engine\n(pure, no DB)"]
    CERT["3. Certificates\nlargest module, 5 tables"]
    DEF["4. Deficiencies\n4-state status"]
    CREW["5. Crew + crew certs\n(+ scrub-PII, Phase 4)"]
    INS["6. Insurance"]
    ISM["7. ISM Templates"]
    MAN["8a. Manuals"]
    DRW["8b. Drawings"]
    MEF["9. Monthly Executed Forms"]
    INTEG["10. Vessel-detail\nintegration pass"]
    ALERTS["11. Alerts aggregator"]
    REM["12. Reminders"]
    DASH["13. Dashboard"]
    SET["14. Settings\n(System Lists, General, etc.\n- no auth needed)"]
    USERROLES["14a. Users & Roles\n(Settings sub-page)"]
    NOTIF["Notifications\n(real userId FK from day one)"]
    EXPORT["15. Export to Excel/PDF"]
    EMAIL["16. Email digest\n(Admin daily digest, new)"]

    AUTH --> V
    V --> SP
    V --> CERT
    V --> DEF
    V --> CREW
    V --> INS
    V --> ISM
    V --> MAN
    V --> DRW
    AUTH --> NOTIF
    V --> NOTIF
    AUTH --> USERROLES

    ENG --> CERT
    ENG --> CREW
    ENG --> INS
    ENG -. "deficiencies use a fixed rule, not a type table" .-> DEF

    CERT --> INTEG
    CREW --> INTEG
    INS --> INTEG

    DEF --> ALERTS
    CERT --> ALERTS
    CREW --> ALERTS
    INS --> ALERTS

    ISM --> MEF
    ISM --> SET

    ALERTS --> DASH
    MEF --> DASH
    DEF --> DASH
    MAN --> DASH

    CERT --> EXPORT
    DEF --> EXPORT

    ALERTS --> EMAIL
    SET --> EMAIL
    NOTIF -. "same alert signal, different channel - not a build dependency" .-> EMAIL

    classDef done fill:#5DCAA5,stroke:#27500A,color:#0B1526
    classDef foundation fill:#378ADD,stroke:#0D2B45,color:#fff
    class V done
    class AUTH foundation
